    "updated_at": "2025-04-21T16:54:34Z",
    "body": "While this would be nice if this form was being designed from scratch, it's unlikely to be viable due to the Web's backwards compatibility commitment. That is to say, removing `<link rel=\"stylesheet\"` is off the table and given that fact, adding `<style src=\"\"` to do semantically the exact same thing doesn't have as strong of an argument imo.\n\nadditionally, if it made it in it would have to be `<style src=\"/styles.css\"></style>` since whether or not `<style>` is a void tag can't change based on context.",
